\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 What actually reduces scam/bad-actor risk on a marketplace\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf0 Given MapIt's context \'97 you already have Claude-based listing moderation and Supabase RLS in place \'97 OTP should be treated as just the front door, not the security system. The layers that actually matter for trust & safety:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Rate-limiting & device/IP fingerprinting at signup
\f1\b0  \'97 flag many accounts from one device or IP in a short window.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Progressive trust levels
\f1\b0  \'97 new accounts get limited listing visibility/reach until they build history (first transaction, positive feedback), rather than full trust from OTP alone.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Optional stronger KYC for sellers
\f1\b0  \'97 e.g., linking a listing to a verified name (via a lightweight ID check) once transaction value crosses a threshold, rather than gating all signups behind it.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Report/block + your existing moderation pipeline
\f1\b0  \'97 catches bad listings and bad actors after the fact, which is realistically where most scam prevention happens on any classifieds platform (OLX, Craigslist included).\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 In-app chat with no upfront phone-number exposure
\f1\b0  \'97 reduces the payoff for scammers who currently rely on getting a phone number early to run off-platform scams.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \
So: pick WhatsApp OTP for the DLT-avoidance and UX reasons, not because it meaningfully changes your fraud exposure \'97 that's a separate problem your moderation and trust-layer design need to solve regardless of which OTP channel you use.
